meta {
  name: Lead Pull - Run Status
  type: http
  seq: 19
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/meta/lead-pull/runs/{{leadPullRunId}}?tenant_id={{tenantId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: auth_token={{authToken}}
}

docs {
  What the screen polls while a pull is in flight, and the delta summary
  afterwards.

  Returns status, filters (as submitted), counts, the timestamps, plus:
    verdict_summary  verdict -> count, the numbers the summary renders
    apply_summary    applied_status -> count, once Apply has run
    importable       how many rows Apply would act on right now
    campaign_filter_is_post_fetch

  counts carries the things a half-answer must not hide:
    truncated / truncated_forms  a form hit the per-form Graph page cap, so
                                 OLDER LEADS IN IT WERE NOT PULLED. Surface this
                                 LOUDLY — it is the difference between "nothing
                                 is missing" and "we stopped looking".
    page_errors                  pages absent from /me/accounts, WITH the reason
                                 (usually: the Page moved to another Business, or
                                 the token lost access). Never swallowed.

  The verdicts, in the order they are decided:
    already_synced   meta_lead_id already in ext.meta_leads
    test_lead        Lead Ads Testing Tool placeholder data
    unmapped_form    no active ext.meta_page_form_org_map row (org_id IS NULL)
    missing_contact  no phone value for any configured phone key
    phone_duplicate  IMPORTABLE — the write path supersedes on phone
    email_duplicate  IMPORTABLE — the write path treats it as a re-submission
    new              IMPORTABLE

  NOTE: `hiring_form` is NOT a verdict here, unlike the Python original. Since
  campaign types (schema 1.49.0) a hiring lead has somewhere to go, so it became
  the is_hiring_form / suggested_campaign_type_id columns instead and such leads
  now import. See Lead-Pull-List-Run-Leads.bru.

  Regression checks:
    * already_synced count must equal
        SELECT count(*) FROM ext.meta_leads WHERE meta_lead_id IN (<those ids>)
    * pull a window overlapping a lead the webhook already ingested -> it
      classifies already_synced, and is NOT offered for import
    * a run id from tenant B, requested as tenant A -> 404, not 403 and not data
    * a bogus tenant_id -> 404 "Tenant not found"
    * caller below super_admin -> 403
}
